  {
   "claim_id": "C3",
   "text": "QUIC's head-of-line blocking elimination only improves latency when multiple concurrent streams experience packet loss simultaneously. Production analysis shows HOL blocking removal rarely moves the needle on real page loads because most pages lack enough concurrent streams hitting loss at the same time. Application-level request dependencies also persist: if high-priority work waits on low-priority data, the transport layer isolation provides no relief. QUIC's advantage concentrates in multi-stream video/image loads and distributed APIs, not single-request workloads.",
